WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:31.166
In the previous verses,

2
00:00:31.166 --> 00:00:33.875
Lord Krishna described His divine nature

3
00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:36.916
and all-pervading presence.

4
00:00:36.916 --> 00:00:39.291
Now in this verse, Lord Krishna

5
00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:41.250
sheds light on the transformative power

6
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.041
of devotion.

7
00:00:43.041 --> 00:00:45.416
He addresses the question –

8
00:00:45.416 --> 00:00:49.125
if a devotee commits sinful acts,

9
00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:52.458
can they still be considered a saint?

10
00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:55.541
Lord Krishna assures us that devotion,

11
00:00:55.541 --> 00:00:58.958
when unwavering and centred on Him alone,

12
00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:02.541
elevates and purifies even those

13
00:01:02.541 --> 00:01:06.000
who sometimes fall in their conduct.

14
00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:12.625
In this verse,

15
00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:15.083
Lord Krishna declares

16
00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:19.041
that even if a devotee commits
the most condemnable act,

17
00:01:19.041 --> 00:01:21.958
they should still be considered a saint –

18
00:01:21.958 --> 00:01:24.500
if their devotion is unwavering.

19
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.500
This statement reveals the power of devotion,

20
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.958
which goes beyond ordinary moral standards.

21
00:01:30.958 --> 00:01:32.125
Here, Lord Krishna

22
00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.791
values the sincerity of the devotee's resolve

23
00:01:34.791 --> 00:01:38.125
more than their temporary lapses.

24
00:01:38.125 --> 00:01:41.208
But this is not permission
for someone on the path

25
00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:44.541
of devotion to engage in sinful acts.

26
00:01:44.541 --> 00:01:46.375
Certainly not.

27
00:01:46.375 --> 00:01:47.375
This verse

28
00:01:47.375 --> 00:01:50.416
refers to errors that occur due to unavoidable

29
00:01:50.416 --> 00:01:54.958
circumstances – accidental missteps.

30
00:01:54.958 --> 00:01:57.958
Lord Krishna in this verse says –

31
00:01:57.958 --> 00:01:58.791
'sadhur eva

32
00:01:58.791 --> 00:02:00.625
sa mantavyah,'

33
00:02:00.625 --> 00:02:04.875
meaning such a devotee should
be considered a saint.

34
00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:06.750
Lord Krishna clearly states

35
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.750
that other people

36
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.833
should set aside

37
00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:12.083
those actions of his and regard him as a saint.

38
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:14.875
And this instruction is not optional –

39
00:02:14.875 --> 00:02:18.083
it is Lord Krishna's own command.

40
00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:19.958
And to disregard it

41
00:02:19.958 --> 00:02:23.041
would be to defy Lord Krishna's authority.

42
00:02:23.041 --> 00:02:25.291
The key quality of such a devotee

43
00:02:25.291 --> 00:02:27.208
is their 'ananya-bhak,'

44
00:02:27.208 --> 00:02:29.208
meaning toward Lord Krishna

45
00:02:29.208 --> 00:02:31.291
to practise exclusive devotion,

46
00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:34.791
without other paths or objects of worship

47
00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:36.541
distracting them.

48
00:02:36.541 --> 00:02:37.500
But

49
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.750
Lord Krishna is not

50
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:42.083
endorsing sinful behaviour. Rather

51
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:43.458
in material conditions

52
00:02:43.458 --> 00:02:46.208
He acknowledges the human struggle

53
00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:47.208
and unwavering

54
00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:47.791
devotion's

55
00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:51.000
redeeming power He affirms.

56
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:51.916
That song of liberation –

57
00:02:51.916 --> 00:02:55.250
the power of devotion is what supports it.

58
00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.750
Such a devotee due to past nature

59
00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.291
or weakness may stray from the path.

60
00:03:01.291 --> 00:03:02.541
But Lord Krishna's

61
00:03:02.541 --> 00:03:04.791
service – the resolve to serve Him –

62
00:03:04.791 --> 00:03:05.541
ensures his

63
00:03:05.541 --> 00:03:08.250
ultimate purification.

64
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.458
Lord Krishna's role,

65
00:03:10.458 --> 00:03:12.416
as the compassionate Lord,

66
00:03:12.416 --> 00:03:14.333
is to lift His devotees

67
00:03:14.333 --> 00:03:16.416
and protect them.

68
00:03:16.416 --> 00:03:17.458
Toward higher spiritual

69
00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:20.791
standards of conduct to lead them,

70
00:03:20.791 --> 00:03:23.125
He guides them.

71
00:03:23.125 --> 00:03:24.083
This verse

72
00:03:24.083 --> 00:03:26.708
also reveals Lord Krishna's loving

73
00:03:26.708 --> 00:03:29.833
relationship with His devotees.

74
00:03:29.833 --> 00:03:31.583
He does not abandon them

75
00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:34.208
when devotees falter.

76
00:03:34.208 --> 00:03:37.541
Rather, He strengthens their resolve

77
00:03:37.541 --> 00:03:38.458
and them above their

78
00:03:38.458 --> 00:03:42.375
shortcomings He helps to rise.

79
00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:44.708
The moon's often used

80
00:03:44.708 --> 00:03:47.541
example is fitting here.

81
00:03:47.541 --> 00:03:49.875
Though it may have spots,

82
00:03:49.875 --> 00:03:51.333
its light remains

83
00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:54.375
radiant and unblemished.

84
00:03:54.375 --> 00:03:56.166
Ultimately, this verse

85
00:03:56.166 --> 00:03:59.833
is a testimony to the
transformative power of devotion.

86
00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:01.958
It assures us

87
00:04:01.958 --> 00:04:03.958
that Lord Krishna's love and grace

88
00:04:03.958 --> 00:04:05.875
are accessible to all,

89
00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:08.625
who sincerely seek Him,

90
00:04:08.625 --> 00:04:11.291
in their past and present struggles,

91
00:04:11.291 --> 00:04:14.500
even after the errors they have made.

92
00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.750
Devotion, when genuine and unwavering,

93
00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.458
becomes the vehicle for an eternal

94
00:04:20.458 --> 00:04:22.708
bond with the Lord.

95
00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:30.166
Have you ever wondered

96
00:04:30.166 --> 00:04:34.541
whether after you make a mistake

97
00:04:34.541 --> 00:04:38.541
your worth diminishes?

98
00:04:38.541 --> 00:04:41.000
In human life, the cycle of falling

99
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.250
and rising keeps moving.

100
00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:48.166
It is an unavoidable part of human existence.

101
00:04:48.166 --> 00:04:51.750
But we must learn this –

102
00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.583
when someone stumbles,

103
00:04:54.583 --> 00:04:58.500
they should not be written off,

104
00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.958
because more important than the fall

105
00:05:02.958 --> 00:05:06.541
is to rise again, to learn again,

106
00:05:06.541 --> 00:05:10.375
and to resolve to make a better effort.

107
00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:13.458
When you make mistakes,

108
00:05:13.458 --> 00:05:17.333
do not drown in the sea of guilt.

109
00:05:17.333 --> 00:05:22.041
Instead, acknowledge your mistake

110
00:05:22.041 --> 00:05:24.833
and on the path of growth

111
00:05:24.833 --> 00:05:27.208
strive to move forward.

112
00:05:27.208 --> 00:05:30.375
Remember, I

113
00:05:30.375 --> 00:05:33.791
look not at your momentary lapses,

114
00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:38.708
but at the sincerity of your heart.

115
00:05:38.708 --> 00:05:43.708
Think about this – a seeker sits in meditation,

116
00:05:43.708 --> 00:05:46.791
but the stream of thoughts

117
00:05:46.791 --> 00:05:51.250
keeps pulling them away again and again.

118
00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.500
Should they give up the practice?

119
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.333
No.

120
00:05:56.333 --> 00:06:00.166
They must try again and again.

121
00:06:00.166 --> 00:06:03.375
That is the essence of sadhana.

122
00:06:03.375 --> 00:06:06.333
If you are committed to change

123
00:06:06.333 --> 00:06:08.291
from the heart,

124
00:06:08.291 --> 00:06:12.000
if you desire your own growth,

125
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.041
and for this you stay focused on Me,

126
00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:18.208
then I will always

127
00:06:18.208 --> 00:06:21.666
guide your way.

128
00:06:21.666 --> 00:06:25.833
And this teaching is also about this –

129
00:06:25.833 --> 00:06:29.125
that you with others too

130
00:06:29.125 --> 00:06:31.208
should behave in the same way.

131
00:06:31.208 --> 00:06:35.250
If someone in your life makes a mistake,

132
00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.958
give them the chance to grow,

133
00:06:37.958 --> 00:06:40.833
to recover.

134
00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.833
Offer them support.

135
00:06:42.833 --> 00:06:46.375
Extend forgiveness,

136
00:06:46.375 --> 00:06:49.500
just as I have extended My grace

137
00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:52.708
to all those

138
00:06:52.708 --> 00:06:55.750
who turn toward Me,

139
00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:59.833
whatever their past may have been.

140
00:06:59.833 --> 00:07:02.833
Because true strength

141
00:07:02.833 --> 00:07:05.750
lies in learning, forgiving,

142
00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:10.958
and in helping each other's growth.

143
00:07:15.791 --> 00:07:18.000
In a family, for people

144
00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.250
to make mistakes is natural.

145
00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:25.250
When someone errs, to become angry

146
00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:29.250
or to label them wrong is easy.

147
00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:34.166
But when someone strays from the path,

148
00:07:34.166 --> 00:07:35.291
then they

149
00:07:35.291 --> 00:07:37.583
by their one mistake alone

150
00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:40.166
should not be defined.

151
00:07:40.166 --> 00:07:43.166
In such a situation, what matters

152
00:07:43.166 --> 00:07:45.750
is their willingness,

153
00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:46.583
how

154
00:07:46.583 --> 00:07:50.708
intensely they wish to correct themselves

155
00:07:50.708 --> 00:07:53.708
and in the right direction

156
00:07:53.708 --> 00:07:57.958
to try again they are eager.

157
00:07:57.958 --> 00:08:00.000
Just as fire

158
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.875
purifies metal,

159
00:08:02.875 --> 00:08:06.083
in the same way difficulties can strengthen

160
00:08:06.083 --> 00:08:09.083
the unity of a family.

161
00:08:09.083 --> 00:08:11.000
If a family member

162
00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.125
does something inappropriate,

163
00:08:14.125 --> 00:08:17.666
before reacting, pause,

164
00:08:17.666 --> 00:08:20.541
and instead of punishing them,

165
00:08:20.541 --> 00:08:24.541
help them recover from it.

166
00:08:24.541 --> 00:08:28.500
Offer guidance and support.

167
00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.791
This approach

168
00:08:29.791 --> 00:08:33.416
deepens family bonds.

169
00:08:33.416 --> 00:08:36.833
It teaches everyone that love

170
00:08:36.833 --> 00:08:38.666
and forgiveness

171
00:08:38.666 --> 00:08:42.291
are deeply connected to each other.

172
00:08:42.291 --> 00:08:43.625
When you

173
00:08:43.625 --> 00:08:46.083
instead of blaming,

174
00:08:46.083 --> 00:08:50.000
focus your attention on helping,

175
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:54.958
then you create such an environment

176
00:08:54.958 --> 00:08:57.041
where every person

177
00:08:57.041 --> 00:08:59.541
feels safe to learn from their mistakes

178
00:08:59.541 --> 00:09:03.958
and to grow.

179
00:09:03.958 --> 00:09:06.750
And this is the essence

180
00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:10.208
of a happy and peaceful family life.

181
00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:18.708
At the workplace, mistakes

182
00:09:18.708 --> 00:09:21.708
are inevitable.

183
00:09:21.708 --> 00:09:25.916
But as a leader,

184
00:09:25.916 --> 00:09:30.166
how do you respond to these mistakes, 

185
00:09:30.166 --> 00:09:36.166
shapes the work culture you build.

186
00:09:36.166 --> 00:09:41.250
Even if someone strays from the path,

187
00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:44.916
what matters more here

188
00:09:44.916 --> 00:09:49.541
is their firm desire to learn and improve,

189
00:09:49.541 --> 00:09:54.750
not just the mistake they made.

190
00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:55.916
If you

191
00:09:55.916 --> 00:09:59.541
only promote a culture of punishment,

192
00:09:59.541 --> 00:10:01.833
then you create

193
00:10:01.833 --> 00:10:05.750
a culture of fear and avoidance,

194
00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.291
whereas

195
00:10:07.291 --> 00:10:09.875
forgiveness nurtures growth

196
00:10:09.875 --> 00:10:12.791
and trust.

197
00:10:12.791 --> 00:10:14.750
When a colleague,

198
00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.625
an employee

199
00:10:16.625 --> 00:10:20.375
makes a mistake at the workplace,

200
00:10:20.375 --> 00:10:23.000
then their intentions

201
00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:26.416
and circumstances – consider them.

202
00:10:26.416 --> 00:10:28.125
Did it happen

203
00:10:28.125 --> 00:10:32.666
that even after their best effort,

204
00:10:32.666 --> 00:10:35.666
due to their inexperienced

205
00:10:35.666 --> 00:10:39.208
approach to the work, a mistake occurred,

206
00:10:39.208 --> 00:10:44.208
and they were judged unfairly?

207
00:10:44.208 --> 00:10:48.333
In such cases, instead of removing them

208
00:10:48.333 --> 00:10:52.375
from the workplace, you can teach them

209
00:10:52.375 --> 00:10:56.833
how to approach the work
in a more balanced way.

210
00:10:56.833 --> 00:10:59.291
The meaning of this approach

211
00:10:59.291 --> 00:11:02.541
is not to tolerate carelessness,

212
00:11:02.541 --> 00:11:09.625
but it means to balance
responsibility with empathy.

213
00:11:09.625 --> 00:11:13.458
When you lead in this way,

214
00:11:13.458 --> 00:11:17.000
you inspire loyalty

215
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:20.375
and create such an environment

216
00:11:20.375 --> 00:11:23.833
where every person

217
00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:26.750
strives for excellence.

218
00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.500
Ultimately,

219
00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.708
we are all seekers striving on the path

220
00:11:31.708 --> 00:11:35.833
of karma, and to realise our highest

221
00:11:35.833 --> 00:11:38.750
potential,

222
00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:42.791
we need each other's support.
